WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.140
BETH: For most people, going to the doctor
or dentist is a routine experience, but

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.859
for individuals with autism, accessing
health and care support can be a

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.049
difficult and stressful experience.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.059
JOE: New environments and sensory changes
can be challenging and cause anxiety.

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:19.559
It’s important that healthcare
professionals, are aware of the needs

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.030
for those with autism, and are able to
make the experience easier to handle.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.419
Health and care settings should also
provide more flexibility, to adapt

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.309
to the needs of people with autism.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.399
BETH: GPs should have a good
understanding and knowledge

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.160
about autism, and the appropriate
services to refer individuals to.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.970
Appointments should also be long
enough to meet the communication

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.810
needs of an individual with autism.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.680
JOE: Long waiting times for diagnosis
can put extra pressure on parents and

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.190
carers unnecessary stress to people
with autism, as this may mean longer

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.210
waits for treatment and support.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.810
In some areas, there may be a lack
of support services for people living

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:04.379
with autism, including getting an
education, health and care plan ‘EHC’,

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:08.270
or a lack of information available
to accessing the support they need.

00:01:08.849 --> 00:01:12.890
BETH: A high proportion of children with
autism attend mainstream schools, which

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:17.420
should all endeavour to do their utmost
in providing the necessary support for any

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.750
student who has special educational needs.

00:01:20.099 --> 00:01:23.789
However, the needs of individuals
with autism as we have discussed

00:01:23.789 --> 00:01:27.609
in other units often go further
than extra learning support.

00:01:28.529 --> 00:01:32.520
There are specialist schools available and
other mainstream schools are well-equipped

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.910
with facilities to accommodate students
with autism, but this is not consistent.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.729
JOE: Autism is clearly established as
a learning difficulty requiring special

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:46.899
education provision, and a child with
autism may be eligible for an ‘EHC’

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:51.310
plan once an assessment of their needs
has been made by the local authority.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:56.530
This will describe their needs and
any specialist provision to meet those

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:02.630
needs and can be accessible from 0-25
years as long as they are in education

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.329
or training, but not at university.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.579
The opportunities for progression onto
further education or training will vary

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.670
depending on where an individual lives.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.280
BETH: Every further education
college should provide their students

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.619
with special educational needs,
the extra help that they need to

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.059
support them with their studies.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.969
This includes students
on the autistic spectrum.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.700
The special educational needs
coordinator or SENCO will be in

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.570
charge of organising any extra
learning support or general needs.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.409
JOE: Students with autism may be able
to access extra support at university

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:42.710
through the institution's own additional
needs team, or SEN support team.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.150
This may involve having access
to a specialist service such as a

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:51.570
note-taker during lectures or a mentor
to provide support such as balancing

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:55.489
workloads and accessing social
opportunities and leisure facilities.

00:02:56.139 --> 00:02:58.969
They may also be entitled
to extra time in exams.

00:02:59.359 --> 00:03:03.459
BETH: Engaging in leisure activities
can lower stress levels and improve mood

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:08.320
which can help to increase psychological
engagement and avoid unhealthy behaviours.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:12.940
Sport has so many benefits, not
only as a great way to stay fit,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.489
it can also offer a sense of
belonging and a way to make friends.

00:03:17.059 --> 00:03:21.620
Regularly taking part in sport can provide
routine and structure and is a good

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.549
way to release stress and frustration.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:28.500
Some sports clubs cater specifically for
the needs of individuals with autism.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:33.879
JOE: Visiting the theatre or the cinema
can be exciting, and a great way to

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.630
explore a passion for something, but
also very challenging for individuals

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.300
with autism as they might find it
difficult to cope with big crowds.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:46.559
However, some cinemas run autism friendly
screenings, where they lower sound levels

00:03:46.719 --> 00:03:48.720
and there is more freedom to move around.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:52.640
BETH: Museums can also be a great
place for individuals with autism to

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:56.310
explore their special interests, and
they are a great learning resource.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.359
Many now have interactive displays
which involve all the senses.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.370
JOE: The most important thing about
attending a leisure facility is to

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.660
first see if they have any specific
support already available, and

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:12.690
informing them about the visit, may
help them to give guidance about what is

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.490
available and for them to be prepared.
